Title: "Topic Headers"
Id: "ac992e5d-567c-43ed-95c4-58ae9cb6b25e"

Text: "Topic headers begin with `#` followed by a dotted name path, and are used by
`Topic:` groups.

```mlg-fragment
[#real.analysis]
Topic: \"Analysis over the real numbers.\"
```

The heading renders as a human title by title-casing the path — `#real.analysis`
becomes \"Real Analysis\" — unless the item's `Documented:` `called:` text
overrides it.

Elsewhere a topic is *referred to* as quoted text (`\"#real.analysis\"`) so a
reference is never mistaken for a usage. Those quoted references appear in a
`Topic:` item's `within:` and `Related:` `to:` sections and in a `Relation:`
item's `between:`/`and:` sections."
Id: "e1160b78-1efd-479c-a19d-a8f341d2cc30"
